Cambridge, MA 02138


From ruth at stats.ox.ac.uk  Mon Mar 21 23:46:43 2011
From: ruth at stats.ox.ac.uk (Ruth M. Ripley)
Date: Mon, 21 Mar 2011 22:46:43 +0000 (GMT Standard Time)
Subject: [Rsiena-help] undirected networks in RSiena
In-Reply-To: <4D81117A.1050909@fas.harvard.edu>
References: <4D81117A.1050909@fas.harvard.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.WNT.4.64.1103212241240.8992@sony-PC>

Kevin,

1) There is an option called modelType which is not available via the GUI.
The documentation is rudimentary at the moment, I am afraid. 
?sienaModelCreate will tell you the possible values. I think 3 is what you 
need.

2) It is no longer necessary to use the finite difference method for 
undirected networks.

Hope this helps,

Ruth

